# PlasticOS XML Data & Cron Rules
# Source: .claude/rules/xml-views.md

## Seed Data Rules (Deterministic Seed Doctrine)

- Wrap ALL reference data in `<odoo noupdate="1">` — never plain `<odoo>`
- Every record needs a prefixed external ID: `id="plasticos_{module}.record_name"`
- `❌` Never hardcode database IDs in `ref=""` — always use external IDs
- `❌` Never bootstrap data via CSV at runtime
- `❌` No seed data without external IDs

**Correct pattern:**
```xml
<odoo noupdate="1">
  <record id="plasticos_base.partner_tag_buyer" model="res.partner.category">
    <field name="name">Buyer</field>
    <field name="active" eval="True"/>
  </record>
</odoo>
```

## File Skeleton — `<data>` vs `<data noupdate="1">`

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<odoo>
  <data noupdate="1">
    <!-- reference/seed data — loaded ONLY on first install, never overwritten by -u -->
  </data>
  <data>
    <!-- records that SHOULD re-sync on every upgrade (e.g. views, menus) -->
  </data>
</odoo>
```

`noupdate="1"` is mandatory for all seed/reference data and for `ir.cron` records (see below) — it prevents `make update m=X` from resetting customised or operator-disabled records.

## The `eval` Attribute Context

`eval=` runs a restricted Python expression instead of a literal. Only these names are in scope:

| Name | Meaning | Example |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| `True` / `False` | Python booleans | `eval="True"` |
| `datetime` | `datetime.datetime` | `eval="datetime.now()"` |
| `timedelta` | `datetime.timedelta` | `eval="(datetime.now() + timedelta(days=30)).strftime('%Y-%m-%d')"` |
| `time` | Python `time` module | `eval="time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')"` |
| `ref(xml_id)` | External ID → DB `res_id` (raises if missing) | `eval="ref('base.main_company')"` |

**Compliant patterns:**
```xml
<field name="active" eval="True"/>
<field name="company_id" eval="ref('base.main_company')"/>
<field name="company_id" eval="False"/>            <!-- unset a field -->
<field name="tag_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('plasticos_base.tag_1'), ref('plasticos_base.tag_2')])]"/>
```

For a plain Many2one, prefer the bare `ref` attribute over `eval`:
```xml
<field name="categ_id" ref="product.product_category_all"/>
```

**CI gate (check_odoo_patterns.sh #11):** never nest double quotes inside `eval`. Use single quotes:
- `✅ eval="[ref('plasticos_base.tag_1')]"`
- `❌ eval="[ref(\"plasticos_base.tag_1\")]"` — XML parse failure

**Data load order in `__manifest__.py`** (required sequence):
```
security/*.csv  →  data/*.xml  →  views/*.xml  →  data/*cron*.xml
```

Seed categories (all must be XML with noupdate):
- Partner tags, material taxonomy, payment terms, chart of accounts
- Selection value seeds, ICP defaults, sequence seeds

## Cron (ir.cron) Rules — Odoo 19

> **Generic Odoo vs PlasticOS overrides.** Upstream Odoo 19 docs still show `numbercall`,
> `doall`, `active eval="True"`, and `user_id` = `base.user_root`/`base.user_admin`.
> **Inside this repo those are wrong** — the rules below win and are CI-enforced.

- `❌ numbercall` — removed in Odoo 19; never add to XML (CRON306 + check_odoo_patterns.sh #5)
- `❌ doall` — removed in Odoo 19; never add to XML (CRON305)
- `✅` Always include `interval_number` **and** `interval_type` (CRON307)
- `✅` `state=code` crons must carry a `code` field (CRON308)
- `✅` `user_id` **must** be `plasticos_base.user_system_cron` — `base.user_root` is forbidden (CRON303/CRON304)
- `✅` `model_id` ref **must** carry the module prefix: `ref="plasticos_module.model_plasticos_my_model"` (check_odoo_patterns.sh #10)
- `✅` Default `active` eval="False" for new crons (enable via feature flag or ICP)
- `✅` Wrap cron records in `<odoo noupdate="1">` so `-u` never resets next-run date or re-enables a disabled cron
- Use advisory locks for crons that must not overlap (see `tools/cron_invariant_check.py` CRON2xx lifecycle rules):
  ```python
  if not self.env.cr.execute("SELECT pg_try_advisory_lock(hash)"):
      return  # another cron instance is running
  ```

**Correct cron pattern:**
```xml
<odoo noupdate="1">
  <record id="plasticos_module.cron_my_action" model="ir.cron">
    <field name="name">PlasticOS: My Cron</field>
    <field name="model_id" ref="plasticos_module.model_plasticos_my_model"/>
    <field name="user_id" ref="plasticos_base.user_system_cron"/>
    <field name="state">code</field>
    <field name="code">model.my_cron_method()</field>
    <field name="interval_number">1</field>
    <field name="interval_type">hours</field>
    <field name="active" eval="False"/>
  </record>
</odoo>
```

## The `<function>` Tag (install-time one-shot logic)

Use `<function>` for setup logic that must run **once at install** (not on a schedule).
It is not a cron — do not use it for recurring work.

```xml
<odoo noupdate="1">
  <function model="plasticos.material.profile" name="_seed_default_profiles"/>

  <!-- with positional args -->
  <function model="res.partner" name="_create_partner_with_name">
    <value>Acme Corp</value>
  </function>
</odoo>
```

